  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-09-02T17:41:42.668Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "When you block a user on VRChat, they can still use your avatars and go to your worlds which I feel like this should be changed. \nHere is an example: Lets say a user you have blocked tries to join a world you have made and or use your avatars, they can still do this even though you have blocked them. \n\nHere is my idea of how it should be: If a user you have blocked tries to join a world you have made or wear an avatar you have created, a message should pop up saying, \"You cannot use this avatar/go to this world because the user that has created it has blocked you\" or something along those lines. \n\nI think that this should be implemented because it would make VRChat a safer platfrom for creators. It would also give creators on VRChat more motivation to keep making worlds/avatars because they would know that users they have blocked wouldn't see their content.",
